WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
Speaker 1: You know, usually when I say,&nbsp;
hey, here's what the right is saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:10.160
and here's why it doesn't make sense because it&nbsp;
could happen and B could happen. A and B don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.680
usually happen within like a few days. But&nbsp;
with the entire definition of a woman thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.240
it has now happened with Republican Senator Josh&nbsp;
Hawley. And we're going to look at it because it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:28.160
exactly why I said the idea that it's so simple to&nbsp;
define woman as far as Republicans are concerned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:34.080
really isn't borne out by the actual fact. So&nbsp;
let's backtrack a little bit. When Judge Katju&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.880
Brown Jackson's confirmation hearings were going&nbsp;
on, Senator Marsha Blackburn, a Republican, said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.080
Can you define a woman? And Judge Jackson said,&nbsp;
You know, in the context of legality, I really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.440
can't, because when we figure out if the question&nbsp;
is who can bring a gender discrimination lawsuit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.640
it depends on the specific facts of a case, so&nbsp;
I can't really tell you. And then she went on to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.520
say, I'm also not a biologist, so I can't give&nbsp;
you like a biological definition. I'm a judge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.080
And one of the things I said to you guys was, it's&nbsp;
not as simple as it seems. And within a few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.800
I appeared on the right wing Michael Knowles&nbsp;
show, and he suggested the definition for a woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.960
anyone who's not a man. And of course, that&nbsp;
doesn't really work. It ignores intersex people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.960
And then he said, Well, it's a human that&nbsp;
produces eggs. Well, there's lots of conditions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:22.080
like hormonal imbalances and thyroid conditions&nbsp;
and things in the womb and pituitary tumors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.880
which prevent women from producing&nbsp;
eggs. But they're still women.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:30.720
And then there was well capable of reproduction&nbsp;
through pregnancy. Lots of conditions inhibit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:36.480
reproduction. What about post-menopausal woman?&nbsp;
What about a postmenopausal woman? What about a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.440
woman who has had a hysterectomy? Well, by his?&nbsp;
By that definition, they wouldn't be a woman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:49.280
This brings us to Republican Senator Josh Hawley,&nbsp;
who was recently asked about this. And in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.000
HuffPost asked a bunch of Republican senators,&nbsp;
Can you define woman in? Most of them didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.240
even answer, probably because they realized,&nbsp;
even though we pretended it was really easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.080
for Judge Jackson to answer. We're not&nbsp;
answering either. But Josh Josh Hawley did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:08.720
to his credit. And Josh Hawley initially&nbsp;
said someone who can give birth to a child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:15.920
a mother is a woman. Someone who has a uterus is&nbsp;
a woman. It doesn't seem that complicated to me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:24.480
And so the follow up was What if a woman has her&nbsp;
uterus removed by a hysterectomy? Is she still a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:31.280
woman? And Josh Hawley initially said, Yeah, well,&nbsp;
I don't know. Would they? And the answer was yes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.960
And later, when Josh Hawley was asked, Well,&nbsp;
would you consider a woman to be a woman if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:44.720
she lost her reproductive organs to cancer? Hawley&nbsp;
said, I mean, a woman still has a vagina, right?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.200
Which is a different definition. First, it was&nbsp;
capable of reproduction. Then it was like, Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.800
actually, that's not the definition. It's having a&nbsp;
vagina. And then, of course, there are trans women&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:01.760
who have vaginas. He wasn't asked about that, but&nbsp;
the point here is these definitions don't work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:10.800
in figuring out. Who is a woman for specific&nbsp;
purposes, right? If the question is, who is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:19.760
woman for needing OB-GYN care? Well, there are&nbsp;
definitely some transwomen that don't need an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.680
OB-GYN. But then there's a different question who&nbsp;
is a woman for the purposes of bringing a gender&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.880
discrimination lawsuit? And that's a different&nbsp;
definition. So the most important takeaway is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.320
they want everybody else to think&nbsp;
there's one definition for all contexts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.160
and it's really simple. And anyone who doesn't&nbsp;
give you that definition is being dishonest or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.320
they're being unrealistic or whatever. And&nbsp;
even Josh Hawley's definition that came from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:54.080
him already ran into a bunch of problems needing&nbsp;
him to backpedal. So if we need any reminder that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:59.760
it's not as simple as they make it out to be, we&nbsp;
now have as a data point that Josh Hawley himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.800
who was on those confirmation hearings for Judge&nbsp;
Jackson, although he didn't ask these particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.600
questions. He's already had to revise his&nbsp;
definition. Very interesting data point.

